[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: An LLM renders for human reading until a viewer exists

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[DECISION]
UID: DEC-HITL-IS-THE-VIEWER
TITLE: An LLM renders for human reading until a viewer exists
AUTHORED_BY: human
STATUS: accepted
RETIRES_ON: >>>
A working beads sandbox exists and the viewer that follows it is in use.
<<<
STATEMENT: >>>
Human reading is served by on-the-fly LLM expansion during a working session,
not by a rendered artifact. The operator makes decisions in conversation, and
the model pulls in whatever neighbouring content the decision needs.

Conversion is therefore not gated on a viewer. Order of work is the sdoc plan,
then early beads implementation, then the viewer.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Readability is not the near-term bottleneck. Deciding what is safe to build is.
The single-source-of-truth property and well-defined edges to that truth are
what matter in the early hours; the render is downstream of both and can wait.
<<<
